      "SNOMED-NCIT"
    ],
    "coherence": {
      "note": "Logical coherence of each system's own submitted alignment M (the whole alignment, not only the test slice): 'elk'/'hermit' is the number of unsatisfiable named classes in O_src ∪ O_tgt ∪ M with each correspondence asserted as EquivalentClasses; the incoherence degree is that count over union_class_count. Computed organiser-side with ROBOT 1.9.10. ELK is a sound lower bound; HermiT is exact and is run on NCIT-DOID only.",
      "conventions": [
        "Only '=' correspondences are asserted, with the same rule for RDF and TSV submissions.",
        "A correspondence is dropped if either endpoint is owl:deprecated or is not a class of its task ontology.",
        "DOID is loaded without the classes and axioms of its ext.owl imports; only the imports' object- and annotation-property declarations are kept, so that DOID's own axioms parse unchanged.",
        "Deprecated classes and OWL API placeholder classes are excluded from both numerator and denominator."
      ],
